flowchart TB
  accTitle: How the Workflow test runs the reusable workflows
  accDescr: Every pull request, every push to main and a run by hand start the Workflow test. Its first job asks GitHub for the files of a pull request: one that changes nothing that the dry runs run or read skips the calls. Otherwise one job calls each reusable workflow of the commit as a repository does, with the permissions of its template and as a dry run, also from a fork with a token that can only read. Before its checkouts, every job of a reusable workflow stops when GitHub names no commit of the workflow. The labels, the findings and the lifecycle run in full; the issues run with the input smoke, whose job event takes the canary's issue, whose analyze is skipped and whose apply checks the answer of tests/fixtures/smoke-answer.json; the discussions get no event of theirs and skip every job. The last job, the required check reusable workflows, reads the jobs of the run: each one passed with the step that writes the plan of its dry run, or was skipped where its call has to skip it, and it fails on every other.
  start(["a pull request, a push<br>to main, or by hand"]) --> changes{"`**what the reusable workflows run**:<br>does it change what the<br>dry runs run or read?`"}
  changes -- "no" --> skipped["every call skipped"]
  changes -- "yes" --> calls["`**one call per reusable workflow**:<br>the permissions of its template,<br>dry_run, also from a fork`"]
  calls --> guard{"each job: does GitHub<br>name the commit<br>of its workflow?"}
  guard -- "no" --> red["the check fails,<br>with what to fix"]
  guard -- "yes" --> full["`**labels, findings, lifecycle**:<br>each in full, as a dry run`"]
  guard -- "yes" --> issues["`**issues**, input smoke:<br>the canary's issue, no AI,<br>apply checks the answer of a file`"]
  guard -- "yes" --> discussions["`**discussions**: no event<br>of theirs, every job skipped`"]
  fixture[("tests/fixtures/<br>smoke-answer.json")] --> issues
  full --> gate
  issues --> gate
  discussions --> gate
  skipped --> gate
  gate{"`**reusable workflows**: did each<br>job pass with its plan, or<br>skip where it has to?`"}
  gate -- "no" --> red
  gate -- "yes" --> green["the required check passes"]
  classDef trigger fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  classDef safe fill:#1a7f3726,stroke:#1a7f37,stroke-width:2px
  classDef untrusted fill:#cf222e26,stroke:#cf222e,stroke-width:2px
  class start,fixture,changes,guard,gate trigger
  class calls,full,issues,discussions,skipped job
  class green safe
  class red untrusted
